he's Joe Thomas the former Browns  all-pro tackle and a Wisconsin grad Joe  you're a former all-pro tackle you're  not considering coming back are you very  happy with retirement and it  I think the knees are a little too far  gone to make any dreams of coming back  and playing well I was one I was being  serious here that you see what's  happening with Cleveland and how hard is  it to look at what's happening in  Cleveland and you went through the tough  years the lean years there with your  career you know any any thoughts like  mentally that you go and I'd like to  come back or I'd love to try to come  back well certainly I wish my career had  more wins than the losses that I was  able to accumulate and obviously it  looks like they're gonna go on a nice  run here they put together a heck of a  team but it's funny I think in my head I  just so certain that I can't do it  anymore  and due to the lack of cartilage and the  pain and suffering that I went through  my last few years just trying to get  ready on Sundays there's nothing in my  mind that says hey maybe if I do this or  that I could get out there and do it I  just know I just don't have anything  left  do you miss hitting people I don't miss  getting it I know that much I'm not sure  I was hitting many people towards the  end of my career anyway I was just  trying to absorb them and get in their  way  for a few seconds so the quarterback  football how much weight have you lost I  would say from my last I'm probably down  about 50 pounds but I surely on in my  career 2012-13 I was pretty heavy I was  like 325 so from that point I'm down  almost 75 but do you get into this mode  that like food is not there to enjoy  like its fuel like I have to eat this  amount not that I want to eat this  amount  yeah I mean that weight was when I was  playing my career I was always sort of  an undersized tackle that had to eat a  lot I mean every meal I had to walk away  feeling like I was going to throw up  just in order to keep enough weight on  so that the coaches weren't yelling at  me on Monday morning so it was always a  struggle I think it became mentally  taxing because every two hours if I  wasn't sitting down and shoving my face  full of bad sugar and carbs and  everything you can imagine I was I would  get stressed out about it because I  would lose weight so quickly when I  would miss a meal that it would it would  be on my mind constantly what was the  bad food that you were shoving into your  mouth well every meal had to have just  an overwhelming amount of carbohydrates  pasta with plenty of dessert which you  know now sounds pretty nice but it also  made my body kind of feel crappy I  always had lots of heartburn and lots of  joint pain from all the sugar and stuff  that I was in taking during my career  well so fight like pizza cookies like  that you you could eat it right yeah  example you know eating a nice normal  meal of an entire plate of lasagna but  then for dessert you need a couple  cookie but that wasn't it then before  bed I would actually go downstairs and  I'd usually pour myself nice 20 or 30  ounce glass a whole milk and then about  a pint of ice cream and then I'd washed  it down with some casein protein before  bed now is really just to maintain my  weight that was about all I had to do  what if you had a maximum weight that  you could that you could weigh in the  NFL just just to maybe encourage guys to  get healthier to be healthier what do  you think about that I'm not sure that  would work it's funny because it seems  like about half the guys that I played  with on the offensive defensive line  were always really struggling and  working hard to gain weight to be able  to get up to that three  pounds or wherever the coach is one of  them and then the other half of the guys  were really struggling hard and you know  we're eating three salads a day just to  get under 325 or 330 so I guess it all  kind of depended on the type of person  you are but you look back in the 80s I  mean there was hardly anybody over 300  pound the N or now it's it's most of the  linemen shoot if you're not 300 pounds  you're under sized uh be put on your  analyst hat here not the former Browns  all-pro tackle here you look at the  brown what what's your biggest concern  about the Browns next season well I  think the big concern going in is just  expectations right the Browns team  hasn't dealt with such an off season of  adulation like they've had right now and  so how does this team handle that I mean  a lot of these guys are young and  they're new and so they haven't been  around for the the decades of losing and  some of the other times when there were  some expectations but I mean there's  legitimate hope that this is a Super  Bowl contender and there's a lot of  people are going to be picking them to  win the AFC North myself included and so  I think just as a young team how do you  handle those heightened expectations how  do you handle that anticipation that  they are going to be good because  they're not sneaking up on anybody  anymore man they won seven games last  year and I think people were a little  surprised by that but they're not  surprising anybody anymore so how do  they handle that how do they put their  nose to the grindstone and go to work  this offseason you got a chance for the  Monday Night Football booth nobody's  been talking to me directly and I'm not  sure I'm ready for that I'm not sure I'm  excited to step into Jason Wynn's shoes  it looks like he didn't have a lot of  fun last year and I'm looking for  something that's fun well do you think  that's a cautionary I mean you being  serious that you saw what happened to  Witten and you're like you know I've  never called a game and to be thrown in  there and now you're following up Witten  so they're they're expecting something  from that person who steps in that booth  yeah you know I auditioned for it last  year and coming out of the audition  after you kind of ask the questions  about alright you know what's it like if  you're doing this you know what's the  preparation like what's the travel like  and you start hearing about it and it's  like wow that's a lot more work than I  did during my career you know when  you're traveling Friday to Tuesday for  20 straight weeks and the two days  you're home you're largely kind of  preparing and especially for somebody  like me who's never called a game I got  a lot of work to do right as an analyst  as somebody that does  you know pregame or you're talking about  the game on one of the highlight shows  that's easy stuff you know that stuff  that you've done throughout your career  because you're just answering questions  from you know what you were used to  doing during your career after games but  when you're calling a game that's a  whole different am on so I'd have a lot  to learn it would be it would be a lot  more work than I'm looking for right now  I'm looking for something pretty easy  dan I don't want to work too hard my  first few years in retirement I respect  that your reaction when you saw Johnny  manziel's now a member of the IAF's  Memphis Express yeah it's interesting  I'm curious to see where that career is  gonna lead him and you know it'll be  interesting to kind of fall on that path  and see what happens you didn't have to  wait a minute  anytime much to say about that in  Chicago and certainly wish him the best  but it won't be the first thing that  shows up on my timeline that's for sure  you got your bracket you're the first  one to turn in your bracket in the  celebrity bracket challenge you got Duke  Gonzaga  Tennessee and Kentucky and Duke winning  the national title how much college  basketball do you watch you you know to  be honest I follow the Badgers and watch  some of the Big Ten stuff and then other  than that I don't really pay much  attention until the tournament rolls  around so uh  timing right now that I'm on your show  talking yes well because I am kind of  the resident expert well we're gonna  find out great to talk to you and we  will keep an eye on those brackets  thanks for joining us as always Joe damn  that's a Joe Thomas former Cleveland  Browns offensive line for more Dan  Patrick show to the audience channel 239  on DirecTV or download the Dan Patrick  show app  [Music]

